NNAAMMEE
     bbssppaattcchh — apply a patch built with bsdiff(1)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     bbssppaattcchh _o_l_d_f_i_l_e _n_e_w_f_i_l_e _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbssppaattcchh utility generates _n_e_w_f_i_l_e from _o_l_d_f_i_l_e and _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e where
     _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e is a binary patch built by bsdiff(1).

     The bbssppaattcchh utility uses memory equal to the size of _o_l_d_f_i_l_e plus the
     size of _n_e_w_f_i_l_e, but can tolerate a very small working set without a dra‐
     matic loss of performance.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     bsdiff(1)

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     Colin Percival <_c_p_e_r_c_i_v_a_@_F_r_e_e_B_S_D_._o_r_g>

BBUUGGSS
     The bbssppaattcchh utility does not verify that _o_l_d_f_i_l_e is the correct source
     file for _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e.  Attempting to apply a patch to the wrong file will
     usually produce garbage; consequently it is strongly recommended that
     users of bbssppaattcchh verify that _o_l_d_f_i_l_e matches the source file from which
     _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e was built, by comparing cryptographic hashes, for example.
     Users may also wish to verify after running bbssppaattcchh that _n_e_w_f_i_l_e matches
     the target file from which _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e was built.

